<title>JAPAN: Daifuku shares lower on takeover plan.</title>
<headline>Daifuku shares lower on takeover plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Daifuku Co Ltd fell on Friday morning, due to a belief that it may be burdened financially by its plan to buy Vanderlande Industries BV of the Netherlands for more than 10 billion yen, traders said.</p>
<p>The news of the takeover was announced on Thursday. Daifuku is a maker of sophisticated materials-handling equipment.</p>
<p>The share price was down 80 yen at 1,320 yen at 0150 GMT, on volume of 122,000 shares.</p>
</text>
